mantle rm540
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_oskar_wickmarsh
title the tart on the landing
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant humour=dry
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk imagines_a_plum_tart_banking_at_each_turn_of_the_stair
likes plum_tart evening_line market_bustle summer_evenings
dislikes cold_tea rats
fears the_house_factors_claim_swallowing_the_last_slice
hopes an_evening_landing_with_time_for_two
topics work +0.6 food +0.5 prices +0.4 pastimes +0.3
styles comfort=share gossip=reserved refuse=measured tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# calculates stair turns by imagining a plum tart balanced on the landing, reserving one slice for the closing hour.

words
oath! = Four runaway plums | A tart on a tilt
saying! = Corner before speed | Leave a slice for the landing
tartbank = a modest tilt | the pastry's bank
plumeye = the dark plum centre | a glistening purple spot
slicemoon = a pastry crescent | a short curved slice
doubletread = a double stride | the paired rise
levelstop = a quiet landing | the level breath
traylip = a raised rim | the modest edge
wetshoe = a wet sole | the glossy tread
duepiece = a slice spoken for | the factor's portion
marketroar = a busy hum | the crowded music
lastcast = a still evening cast | the quiet line
coldercup = a stagnant cup | the lukewarm insult
sometrim = a careful cuff | the folded linen
paststrip = a dry edge | a little rim of crumbs
upperend = the last rise | the final high turn
balancepoint = a level moment | the lifted pause
latchspace = a door's swing | the free arc

any
opinion houses mixed 0 : A factor's due date descends the stairs rather faster than wages climb them.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : My price for a tart concerns the quantity of plum and let the gilding on the window pay for itself.
opinion newcomers for 1 : A new servant ought to hear about the awkward turn before attempting the stairs under observation.
opinion road for 1 : Walking on a surface someone has kept level can be a remarkable act of public generosity.
opinion church for 1 : A peaceful bench where no one needs serving gives me time to return thanks properly.
opinion dole for 1 : A warm portion can give a tired wolf much more than its weight on paper suggests.
opinion city for 1 : From a landing in this city one can hear both the very fine bells and the ordinary business that feeds them.
opinion festivals for 1 : I'd gladly carry a tray down to a festival as long as somebody saves a level spot for my slice.
opinion watch mixed 0 : A clear account delivered soberly beats an impressive race down a staircase.
opinion sump mixed 0 : Low doors can be as carefully attended as high ones. The rain just gives the low ones extra work.

grown
line greet : Welcome to this level patch. | A greeting from a wolf briefly at rest.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A fresh arrival may claim the unoccupied side. | Come inside the arc of this door.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The first rise still has a little novelty. | Daylight has inspected the trays before me.
line greet.return : Yes, hello. My imaginary tart is steady now. | There's one interval between my actual errands.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A friend is always welcome on this landing. | Your arrival improves the prospect from the turn.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : An evening greeting from the last level patch. | At this hour I can take the single treads.
line again.open : Another lap of the same civil staircase. | Back before my imaginary plum has shifted.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Come see the bend from this angle! | A free space for you on the level end!
line farewell : A level road for whatever you're carrying. | May the last stair treat your tired foot kindly.
line farewell.return : I'll steward the remains of the landing. | Step away before the next tray arrives.
line react.news : A measured account will come up quite comfortably. | Tell the part that survived the turn intact.
line react.news.new : That's a new slice on my plate. | I'd allotted no place to that item till now.
line react.news.known : I've had a portion just that shape. | It reached my landing on an earlier journey.
line react.news.doubt : That account leans heavily to one side. | I'd put it level before deciding how much it weighs.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : I can stand by while you set that weight down. | Take the seat where no other errand need pass you.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : Excellent. A plum landed exactly where it belonged. | Good news deserves the unbroken piece of pastry.
line ask.how : Has today given you anywhere level to pause? | How is your share of the day's climbing?
line answer.how : Upright with the filling still inside. | Moderately rested by my own generous reckoning.
line decline : I'd have to put two trays on a single hand for that. | What you're asking exceeds my remaining clear portion.
line accept_decline : Then your business stays upon its own plate. | A refusal needn't be carried through another turn.
line preclose : My imaginary tart can wait. The real tasks can't. | The next rise is beginning to look impatient.
line accept_preclose : Your own staircase has a claim on you. | Very well. I'll keep the passage free.
line thank : You saved me an entire extra climb. Much obliged. | I felt the benefit just where the tray changed hands.
line deflect_thanks : It was a very shallow rise to spare. | I'd already brought a little extra all that way.
line sympathise : Come out of the household traffic while you grieve. | Nobody needs the chair by my landing so much as you do.
line reassure : Reach the first level place before measuring the whole ascent. | I'll take a spare edge if it helps your breathing.
line ack : Yes. That settles level in my hand. | A well-proportioned slice of sense.
line give.advice : Arrange the landing before attempting the grand entrance. | Never judge a stair with both hands full.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family can take the unreserved side of my tray. | A household turn I need no directions for.
line hail [here.time=night] : Stand here above the lamplit tread! | The last bright patch is wide enough for company!
line farewell.return [here.time=dawn] : Fresh light for the first turn of your walk. | Go while the morning has plenty of room.
line assess : The filling stayed within bounds. I'd accept the result. | That judgement will carry past the awkward corner.
line give.opinion : Time for the turn belongs in every estimate of a journey. | A pleasing entrance starts with an uneventful arrival.
line greet [here.weather=rain] : Welcome. The dry portion begins past that tread. | Come off the glazed paving a moment.
line again.open [pair.band=friends] : A second little helping of your company. | Welcome again to my entirely unofficial landing.
line thank [pair.band=friends] : You've earned the slice with the best plum in it. | That favour will travel very comfortably in my memory.
line answer.how [here.time=night] : Tired enough to let the tart carry me upstairs. | Ready for a last slice and the end of my errands.

scene flyingtart
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I judge a turn by what a plum tart would do on a plate carried round it.
b : Why plum in particular? | Are real tarts always available?
a : A plum may shift while the pastry stays put. A very exacting test if you're fond of both. | Only in my imagination. Considerably easier on the household expenses.

scene doublestair
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Unladen, I take two stairs together. With a loaded tray I respect the claims of each individual tread.
b : Doesn't the trick get you there quicker? | Why hurry when empty?
a : The feet arrive quickly. The contents can take an independent route which most households discourage. | I enjoy it. It leaves time at the top to look composed about the whole performance.

scene masterturn
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My learner starts by holding an empty plate and one loose plum. It is a perfectly candid instructor.
b : Does the plum fall? | Who retrieves it?
a : On the first quick turn, quite often. We practise over a cloth so tuition remains affordable. | Usually the learner, having discovered that a small plum can make a considerable return journey.

scene pieturn
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The best slice has one plum almost at the point. You know at once whether your plate is level.
b : Wouldn't it roll off? | Do you eat that bit first?
a : Not in a well-set tart. The movement is slight and altogether sufficient for my calculation. | At home, yes. A serving plate deserves to reach its owner with all its surveying equipment attached.

scene spousecorner
when topic=family self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd save #self.spouse# a spot on the landing with room for two plates and two unoccupied hands.
b : Why the emphasis on hands? | Who gets the outer seat?
a : Serving is a great deal about getting one hand free. I'd like an evening entirely exempt from the rule. | Whichever of us wants a better look at the passing market traffic.

scene debt
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A House factor expects payment when the new moon arrives. I put the amount aside before calculations about luxuries.
b : Even before the tart? | Do you count the days?
a : The saved copper does come out before the pastry. Imaginary slices bear no charge whatsoever. | Evenings, mostly. Wages have an end and a moon has a date, and I need the two to meet.

scene highhouse
when topic=home self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Here in the Heights a stair can make magnificent demands on the very person meant to appear effortless at its summit.
b : Who gets to appear effortless? | Is a high house always like that?
a : Anyone entering with a dish, apparently. The dish should look as though it met no obstacles whatever. | Only a house with stairs and an audience. The hills supply the first part quite freely.

scene workplace
when topic=work self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I check each door's swing while I have an unoccupied hand.
b : What's your test? | Would another hand help?
a : Open it while empty. An inexpensive piece of research frequently overlooked by an eager learner. | When it's available. A sound working method ought also to function on an ordinary day with one servant.

scene evenline
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An evening float is the exact opposite of a service tray. I want it to move when I'm looking away.
b : Why look away? | Does it usually oblige?
a : To enjoy the rest of the water. The line is a reason for a halt as much as a request for fish. | Seldom when observed. My imaginary floating tart would no doubt be more cooperative.

scene marketday
when topic=pastimes self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like the market when every purchase has found its own voice. There's a lovely traffic to an open row.
b : Can you carry things there? | Does all that noise tire you?
a : Quite well if I take my turns early. A straight path belongs only to someone travelling empty. | I can leave it when I like. Noise chosen in leisure feels different from an unexpected household crash.

scene summerend
when topic=weather self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Summer light lingers on the top tread long after the low door has gone into shade.
b : Would you sit there? | Which light do you prefer?
a : Beside it, certainly. I prefer to let other people's journeys continue over the actual stairs. | The narrow bright line along the rim. It lends an ordinary ending a respectable finish.

scene coldtea
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cold tea is what happens when a little refreshment has been made to wait like an unpaid invoice.
b : Should cold tea be returned? | How do you take a cup gone cold?
a : As a guest I'd decline a second cup. As the servant I'd prefer to notice before anybody needed to comment. | Drink it when necessary. An entirely justified grievance can still be rather a small one.

scene rats
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does warn / react.self / assess
a : A plum left under a pantry shelf asks the wrong kind of audience to come in.
b : Do rats really care for plums? | Who should look underneath?
a : They needn't have sophisticated tastes. I'd sooner deny them the opportunity to improve them. | Whoever carried the plate and noticed it had become lighter. That's a short list in my case.

scene roofprayer
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I spare the Bright One my estimates of the stair. A quiet thank-you at the end seems suitable.
b : Do the figures never falter? | What do you give thanks for?
a : Often. A prayer for patience goes down better than an elaborate excuse for my arithmetic. | A day in which the things I carry arrive intact and the shoulders doing the carrying still feel my own.

scene training
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a learner to see the room as the guest sees it, then again as the wolf who must remove everything.
b : What's different on a second look? | Who has the better view?
a : A graceful chair becomes a narrow passage, a polished jug a weight with a slippery handle. | Both are indispensable. A beautiful arrangement can be generous toward either pair of eyes.

scene nightstairs
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At night I slow on the turn even if there's nothing in my hands. An empty plate can be replaced more readily than an ankle.
b : Would an extra lamp help? | Why not count the stairs?
a : In a place where it lights the risers instead of casting my own shadow across them. | Because a foot arriving from the other direction hasn't read my calculations.

scene rainstep
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Wet stone will give my imaginary plum quite an ambitious notion of travel.
b : Could a mat fix that? | Would you use the rail?
a : A flat one that actually lies still, yes. A moving mat adds a second independent passenger. | With an empty hand. I put the load down to get that hand free if I must.

scene oldrule
when topic=lore
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A rule of service worth teaching ought to hold with an ordinary dish on an ordinary evening.
b : What about a state dinner? | Doesn't rank change service?
a : More attention, more hands, the same opinion of gravity. A plum is no respecter of formal occasions. | It changes how many wolves can afford to be offended. It doesn't change how to reach a sound landing.

scene plateprice
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd price a tray by its loaded balance before asking who polished the rim.
b : Could a cheap tray pass? | What does bad balance cost?
a : Certainly. Give it a decent bread heel alongside a brimming cup to prove the point. | Two journeys, a damp floor and the sort of delayed apology that can occupy a whole morning.

scene poorcredit
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My easiest economies begin with the errand that can share another trip. Pairing rises saves less coin than time but both count.
b : Could you carry two loads? | Where might the saved time go?
a : I might take a message in my pocket. I wouldn't use a narrow stair to make a point about my arms. | Find out what the next week's payment really amounts to. An unexplained figure tends to grow in the dark.

scene bossquiet
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd let #self.friend# judge my imaginary tart's balance. I need an opinion from outside my own wrist.
b : Would a friend be too kind? | What's the verdict worth?
a : I trust a familiar eye to enjoy the joke and still notice a tilted plate. | More than an empty compliment when there might be a very real plum to recover.

scene apronwork
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fold one cuff back when serving the tart. Plum filling travels farther than a clerk could reasonably enter in a household account.
b : Do you make the tart too? | Why just one cuff?
a : My present concern is how it reaches the plate. Every household has its own arrangements before that moment. | One carries, one serves. Each hand has a department to supervise.

scene returnnews
when topic=news world.news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Here's an account brought from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. I carried the words without adding to the portion.
b : Can you promise it's complete? | Would you repeat it upstairs?
a : Complete as delivered to me. I'd require a better view before promising anything further. | With its origin. A household hearing the report deserves to see the whole label.

scene courtgossip
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A small remark carried through four doorways is apt to gain the polish of important news.
b : Should a servant keep silent? | Can the account be delivered unpolished?
a : About private household matters, ordinarily. Genuine public news can readily have a source attached. | Pass on the necessary fact and the source, then keep the decorative dish at home.

scene newstaff
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A stranger in service ought to be shown the return route first. Most hosts demonstrate only the magnificent approach.
b : Why the return route? | Is the front door grander?
a : It's often the route a tired learner takes with an armful of empty dishes. A few clear directions earn their time. | Often. The return can be a good deal more inventive in its use of very little space.

scene supperhour
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My own supper tastes best on a plate that has no further appointment elsewhere.
b : Does that change the taste? | Would you eat in the kitchen?
a : It changes how long I give myself to notice the plums. I'd call that a real alteration. | With pleasure if it has a clear seat and no summons attached to my portion.

scene payplan
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first clear evening after that factor's sum is settled will be spent at a genuinely level table.
b : No grand celebration? | Why not the landing?
a : A quiet tart divided without first subtracting anybody else's due seems celebration enough. | A landing encourages the idea that supper intends to go somewhere. I'd prefer it to stay put.

scene measure
when topic=land
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A city's rise is easier to understand after one journey with a full dish and a cup near the rim.
b : Would an empty hand miss it? | What does the cup show?
a : An empty walker can admire the roofline. I rather enjoy that version of the city too. | The exact place where a handsome paved turn slopes toward the drain. Tea has a fine eye for civil works.

scene sorereach
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I change hands when an empty tray begins to feel heavier at one end. My wrist sometimes reports tiredness while my legs still consider the matter open.
b : Would you carry less? | Does a different grip cure it?
a : Yes. A full load poorly held is less useful than two ordinary journeys made safely. | Sometimes rest is the proper answer. No skill in the grip confers an entirely new wrist.

scene latchdream
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If tarts could complain, I suspect the sharpest objection would concern a door which opens toward the carrier.
b : Wouldn't the carrier object first? | Could you blame the door?
a : Possibly. I like to grant the filling an independent view in these discussions. | Only if the hinges changed their minds since morning. More honest to examine my approach.

grown

story fallenplum [topic=work|memories]
  : I practised my grand entrance with one plum on an empty plate. It sat still through the bend and rolled off when I stopped to admire the result.
  : It went straight back downstairs. I made a considerably less grand exit.
  b : Did you recover the plum?
  : Unhurt. Once washed, it earned a retirement more peaceful than its brief career in service.

story firstcast [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I took a little spare line out one evening and parked the float on a wall and surveyed the water. It remained admirably steady.
  : I'd already spent a good while congratulating myself on the calmness of the surface.
  b : Did the fish oblige?
  : I gave the float a chance to meet a real fish before making further claims about the evening.

story billing [topic=prices|memories]
  : I tried dividing a tart on paper so every share was the same size. My sums came out precisely.
  : The real thing had one plum twice as generous as any of the others. Its prospective owner found my arithmetic wanting.
  b : Which slice settled the question?
  : Turned the dish round and let somebody else choose first. A different and cheaper department of mathematics.

story twostep [topic=memories|work]
  : I swept up a fine stair two rises at once and arrived at the top in excellent time. Admired the clear landing, then looked over my shoulder.
  : I'd carefully swept only the even steps.
  b : How was the descent?
  : Slow, comprehensive, and admirably free from any further temptation to demonstrate my efficiency.

story cupsign [topic=food|memories]
  : A little cold tea in a white cup showed me a clear purple streak on the rim. I imagined I'd solved the mystery of a missing plum.
  : The stain was on my own thumb. I'd touched the cup while peering into it.
  b : Did your plum ever appear?
  : It was still on the plate. I was investigating an entirely self-supporting case.

rule @corner
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Level through the turn. Let the plum keep its dignity. | One extra breath for the lip of the tray.

rule @serve
when concept=bark self.job=servant working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Check the swing before bringing the plate forward. | Two stairs when empty, one for a loaded dish.

rule @teaching
when concept=bark self.master=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give that plum enough space to state its objection. | A clear view from the receiver's side first.

rule @supper
when concept=bark self.likes=plum_tart
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A purple eye just shy of the point. Excellent slice. | Set the best filling on a properly level plate.

rule @dark
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The tread's edge deserves a little lamplight. | Slower round the far turn this late.

rule @fish
when concept=bark self.likes=evening_line
does aside
cooldown 8h
say An evening float has quite different duties from a serving dish. | Rest the line where there's room to watch the water.

dlg resident.hub : I've brought my imaginary tart to a level pause. You'll find me available here.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, there's still a seat beside our previous landing.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : The late turn is best taken gently. The approaching turn affords me a short interval.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Stand beyond the tray's swinging room. I'll be quite civil from here.
dlg resident.job [self.job=servant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. A level dish, an unblocked door and no impression of excessive haste.
dlg resident.job : I enjoy duties where small matters of balance visibly contribute to somebody's comfort.
dlg resident.bye : May the last turn take nothing from what you're carrying.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : This household heard that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I set it before you as a received remark.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=no] : Household confidence isn't a dish for me to set out on an empty table.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : From #world.news_from# I received this account. #world.news#. I'll leave the words in their original portion.
dlg master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : #here.trade_title.capitalize#. I can demonstrate why a good servant first looks at where a journey finishes.
dlg master.learn [here.teaches=no] : I already have a learner beside me. A brief question about a level arrival still has room.
dlg master.work : You'll carry, arrange and observe. You'll also receive what somebody else carries so both sides of a service become clear.
dlg master.wages : Training itself doesn't pay wages. It speeds your learning, and anything earned by your completed work stays yours.
dlg master.takes [here.take_on=yes] : I've room to show one learner the turns. Make the request and we'll give it a proper beginning.
dlg master.takes [here.take_on=no] : I can't put you beside me as a learner under the present conditions. #here.take_on_why#.
dlg master.taken : You're taken on. We'll begin with a bare plate and a plum that hasn't learnt discretion.
dlg master.refused : I can't take that arrangement through to the landing today. #topic.why#.
dlg master.bye : Try noticing which way the next service door swings.

graft resident.hub
choice Why do you picture a plum tart on every landing? -> tartangle
node tartangle
say A plate can look quite level until the first turn. A tart has a dark plum at the centre. Picture that moving and you see exactly where to ease your pace.
free
choice What happens when the filling moves in your imagination? -> hiddenplum
choice I can picture the plate now. -> hub
node hiddenplum
say I slow before the real thing shifts. One of the few domestic mishaps it's possible to enjoy in full without troubling the wolf who washes the linen.
choice I hope the linen stays clean. -> hub
choice I'll take my turn carefully. -> bye

graft master.learn
choice Show me how a single plum can teach service. -> plumtrial
node plumtrial
say Centre a plum on a dish. Carry it to a level table and stop. Watch especially what the plum does in the instant you decide the job is finished.
free
choice Why watch after I stop? -> plumfinish
choice I'd like to hear about the work. -> learn
node plumfinish
say Your feet have stopped. The dish may have stopped. A plum that still has a little journey in mind teaches you to finish all three movements together.
choice Let's discuss the learner's place. -> learn
choice I'll try the level table. -> bye
